</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:103.5pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21302v1/err_graph.svg" id="S4.T4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/83;" width="143" height="83"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Real-world compile error rate over all task types</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of neuro-symbolic code verification</span>
Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablation ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Towards Reliable Code-as-Policies: A Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Embodied Task Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports performance across different LLMs used for code generation, evaluated on long-horizon tasks and averaged over <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">High</span> and <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Low Incompleteness</span> conditions. Stronger LLMs improve performance. On average, <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">NeSyRo</span> improves SR by 28.1% and GC by 27.3% over CaP across all LLMs. The SR difference between <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">NeSyRo</span> and the upper-bound <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">NeSyRo</span>-Complete remains at 15.6% on average, indicating that our framework consistently approaches the optimal performance achievable under complete observations. This shows that <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">NeSyRo</span> performs consistently across LLMs. Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablation ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Towards Reliable Code-as-Policies: A Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Embodied Task Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports real-world task failures due to compile errors across task types. <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">NeSyRo</span> consistently exhibits the lowest compile error rate, highlighting the robustness of its verification and validation pipeline. In contrast, CaP w/ CodeSift incurs more compile errors than the base CaP under partial observability, primarily due to hallucinated evaluations by the LLM in the absence of grounded feedback. <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">NeSyRo</span> addresses this issue through environment-aware validation, enabling reliable execution even with incomplete observations.</p>
</div>
